# Figure presentation (companion paper)

Match the empirical house style so the two papers look like a pair.
Author-facing guide: `pef-empirical/documentation/PAPER_FORMATTING.md`.
Canonical checklist: `pef-empirical/.cursor/rules/figures.mdc`.
Implement in this repo's `scripts/generate_figure*.m` (do not copy the empirical pipeline).

## Type

| Element | Size |
|---------|------|
| Axis labels, colourbar labels | 12 pt (minimum 10 pt) |
| Tick labels, contour clabels | 10 pt |
| Panel letters, notes, annotations | 12 pt |
| Legends | 12 pt |

Export at 300 dpi. White figure background.

## Titles and captions

- No axes `title` / `sgtitle` on published figures.
- Narrative lives in the LaTeX caption.
- Captions use (A), (B), (C) to match panel letters. British English.

## Panel letters

- Multi-panel: `(A)`, `(B)`, `(C)` inside the axes, default northwest inset.
- No white patch. 12 pt bold. Another corner only when northwest sits on data.
- Single-panel figures do not need a letter.

## Legends and annotations

- Legends 12 pt, box off, in empty space (not on curves or markers).
- Labels must not overlap each other, data, or panel letters.

## Pre-export check

1. No title on the figure.
2. Panel letters inside the box, same corner across panels.
3. Axis labels 12 pt, ticks 10 pt, annotations and legends 12 pt.
4. Legend and labels clear of data.
5. Caption describes panels without repeating a figure title.
